        ":question/worked-solution": "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\pi }{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})}=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the cotangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $5$ units down. Hence, $D=-5.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=\\frac{3}{2}+(-5)=-\\frac{7}{2}.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{3x}{2})-5.\n$$"
